  ('193237337990053884', 'La Cucaracha', 1934, 'Comedy, Music', 'Lloyd Corrigan, Ray Rennahan, Roy Webb', 'Jack Wagner, John Twist', 'Steffi Duna, Don Alvarado, Paul Porcasi, Eduardo Durant, Eduardo Durant''s Rhumba Band, Sam Appel, Chris-Pin Martin, Julian Rivero', null, 'Señor Martinez, a famous theater owner, visits a local café in Mexico because of its reputation for good food and to audition the famous dancer who performs there. Martinez tells the café owner that if the dancer is as good as he has heard, he will offer the dancer a contract to perform in his theater. The café''s female singer hears about this and is determined that he won''t leave the café without her.', 'Señor Martinez, a famous theater owner, visits a local café in Mexico because of its reputation for good food and to audition the famous dancer who performs there. Martinez tells the café owner that if the dancer is as good as he has heard, he will offer the dancer a contract to perform in his theater. The café''s female singer hears about this and is determined that he won''t leave the café without her.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/xmLPwUN6aDdMOoPNXvy9vdk8JlE.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:177032'),
  ('970592803481198927', 'La Cucaracha', 1959, 'Drama, Romance, War', 'Ismael Rodríguez, Gabriel Figueroa, Mario Llorca', 'Ismael Rodríguez', 'María Félix, Emilio Fernández, Dolores del Río, Antonio Aguilar, Flor Silvestre, Ignacio López Tarso, Cuco Sánchez, Irma Torres', null, 'The Mexican Revolution serves as a backdrop to a torrid love triangle composed of three freedom fighters: a colonel, a widow, and a fiery female soldier.', 'The Mexican Revolution serves as a backdrop to a torrid love triangle composed of three freedom fighters: a colonel, a widow, and a fiery female soldier.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/g64WgIJfROo8lEzv3CY1xPM66Es.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:102634'),
