  ('587725122755289712', 'La Estrella', 2013, 'Drama, Comedy', 'Alberto Aranda', 'Alberto Aranda', 'Ingrid Rubio, Carmen Machi, Marc Clotet, Fele Martínez, Carlos Blanco, Fanny de Castro', null, 'Estrella is a lively girl who works as a cleaner neighborhood and who lives in a modest apartment in Santa Coloma with her boyfriend. His joy and optimism contrasted with adversity around him, especially with the difficult times being experienced co-worker.', 'Estrella is a lively girl who works as a cleaner neighborhood and who lives in a modest apartment in Santa Coloma with her boyfriend. His joy and optimism contrasted with adversity around him, especially with the difficult times being experienced co-worker.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/zXhiDpSADS4FOMFSQTXTlN4WMkE.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:185735'),
  ('1108494270806241245', 'La fame e la sete', 1999, 'Comedy', 'Antonio Albanese, Giulio Manfredonia, Massimo Pau', 'Vincenzo Cerami, Antonio Albanese', 'Antonio Albanese, Lorenza Indovina, Aisha Cerami, Lucia Guzzardi, Rosa Pianeta, Luigi Maria Burruano, Mario Patanè, Béatrice Macola', null, 'Alex, Ivo and Pacifico three Sicilian twin brothers are reunited for their father''s funeral.', 'Alex, Ivo and Pacifico three Sicilian twin brothers are reunited for their father''s funeral.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/xsZq9Nk9HihgJE3HnWScQacfhO.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:62496'),
  ('956835307425723274', 'La famiglia Passaguai', 1951, 'Comedy', 'Aldo Fabrizi, Mario Bava', 'Aldo Fabrizi, Mario Amendola, Ruggero Maccari', 'Aldo Fabrizi, Peppino De Filippo, Ave Ninchi, Luigi Pavese, Nyta Dover, Enrico Luzi, Tino Scotti, Carlo Delle Piane', null, 'When Passaguai family patriarch Giuseppe (Fabrizi) decides to take advantage of a corporate discount to bring his wife (Ninchi) and children to spend a Sunday at the beach of Fiumicino, a series of troubles begins for everyone, in the form of a comic nightmare.', 'When Passaguai family patriarch Giuseppe (Fabrizi) decides to take advantage of a corporate discount to bring his wife (Ninchi) and children to spend a Sunday at the beach of Fiumicino, a series of troubles begins for everyone, in the form of a comic nightmare.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/5Fs2LQQkqxt3YBx0pyLW6qQ3BCt.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:25962'),
  ('10163646486297049', 'La familia bien, gracias', 1979, 'Family, Drama, Comedy', 'Pedro Masó, Andrés Vich', 'Pedro Masó, Rafael Azcona', 'Alberto Closas, José Luis López Vázquez, María José Alfonso, Jaime Blanch, Francisco Benlloch, Margot Cottens, Lola Forner, Tony Fuentes', null, 'Sequel to "The Great Family" and "Family and one more". A widower and the godfather of his 16 children, aged two, wistfully contemplate the past. The father was left alone in the family home, but loneliness overwhelms him so he decides to spend some time at home for each of their children, most of whom are married. But the experience ends up being disastrous.', 'Sequel to "The Great Family" and "Family and one more". A widower and the godfather of his 16 children, aged two, wistfully contemplate the past. The father was left alone in the family home, but loneliness overwhelms him so he decides to spend some time at home for each of their children, most of whom are married. But the experience ends up being disastrous.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/Ajaq5YOvqEV1CaqmtadRPHjoLuc.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:195656'),
