  ('886561279377737321', 'La P’tite Lili', 1927, 'Drama', 'Alberto Cavalcanti', null, 'Catherine Hessling, Jean Renoir, Guy Ferrant, Dido Freire', null, 'La P’tite Lili is a silent short drama depicting the fate of a young orphaned girl in the working-class districts of Paris. The film follows Lili, a teenage girl marked by innocence and vulnerability, as she is drawn into the city’s underworld after encountering a man who exploits her circumstances. Told through impressionistic visual style rather than dialogue, the film presents a tragic portrait of social marginalization and moral collapse within an urban environment.', 'La P’tite Lili is a silent short drama depicting the fate of a young orphaned girl in the working-class districts of Paris. The film follows Lili, a teenage girl marked by innocence and vulnerability, as she is drawn into the city’s underworld after encountering a man who exploits her circumstances. Told through impressionistic visual style rather than dialogue, the film presents a tragic portrait of social marginalization and moral collapse within an urban environment.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/i6Ph3c89LqJuh9zL89GhBiJTKeW.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:123656'),
  ('466123458252488743', 'La paisana Jacinta: En búsqueda de Wasaberto', 2017, null, 'Adolfo Aguilar', null, 'Jorge Benavides', null, 'Jacinta, an Andean indigenous woman, returns to Chongomarca with the mission of finding her husband, Wasaberto. Upon her return, she stumbles upon a multinational construction company that will build a hotel in her modest home.', 'Jacinta, an Andean indigenous woman, returns to Chongomarca with the mission of finding her husband, Wasaberto. Upon her return, she stumbles upon a multinational construction company that will build a hotel in her modest home.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/dDC9LEDeCKTHkYlSFnLmZ8GNAba.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:485390'),
