  ('1140302199334766538', 'Le Bison (et sa voisine Dorine)', 2003, 'Comedy', 'Isabelle Nanty, Philippe Pavans de Ceccatty', 'Fabrice Roger-Lacan', 'Édouard Baer, Isabelle Nanty, Pierre-François Martin-Laval, Nicolas Marais, Tilly Mandelbrot, Marie Martin, Jules-Angelo Bigarnet, Martine Chevallier', null, 'Isabelle Nanty is a Paris concierge, four children to look after and a fifth in gestation with a loutish and uncaring husband who runs off with the girlfried of one of the lodgers in her building. This same lodger called Le Bison has rather strange hours and both he and Dorine ( the concierge ) get on each other''s nerves because each makes noise at the "wrong" time for the other ! The fact that their respective mates have run off together nevertheless bring the two together and with Dorine''s children getting very attached to Le Bison, there are the makings of an "idylle" between the two of them which the return of the two offending mates fails to break', 'Isabelle Nanty is a Paris concierge, four children to look after and a fifth in gestation with a loutish and uncaring husband who runs off with the girlfried of one of the lodgers in her building. This same lodger called Le Bison has rather strange hours and both he and Dorine ( the concierge ) get on each other''s nerves because each makes noise at the "wrong" time for the other ! The fact that their respective mates have run off together nevertheless bring the two together and with Dorine''s children getting very attached to Le Bison, there are the makings of an "idylle" between the two of them which the return of the two offending mates fails to break', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/tmtvyS4Kfe8lYepd1U68C2GZePJ.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:47433'),
  ('1023187991774796285', 'Le Bon Plaisir', 1984, 'Comedy, Drama, Romance', 'Jean Penzer, Francis Girod', 'Françoise Giroud, Francis Girod', 'Catherine Deneuve, Michel Serrault, Jean-Louis Trintignant, Hippolyte Girardot, Michel Auclair, Michel Boisrond, Claude Winter, Alexandra Stewart', null, 'Claire''s handbag is stolen. It contained a letter written ten years previously by the man who is now the French President. In the letter, he urges his pregnant mistress to have an abortion. Claire immediately alerts the President''s men. From that moment, the machinery of state swings into action.', 'Claire''s handbag is stolen. It contained a letter written ten years previously by the man who is now the French President. In the letter, he urges his pregnant mistress to have an abortion. Claire immediately alerts the President''s men. From that moment, the machinery of state swings into action.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rk91V6n6chTeZ4FhBUDndaf9wrU.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:104349'),
  ('51266840677692447', 'Le Bonheur', 1934, 'Comedy, Drama, Romance', 'Jean Dréville, Marcel L''Herbier, Harry Stradling Sr.', 'Marcel L''Herbier, Henri Bernstein, Michel Duran', 'Gaby Morlay, Charles Boyer, Paulette Dubost, Jaque Catelain, Michel Simon, Jean Toulout, Georges Mauloy, Léon Arvel', null, 'Philippe Lutcher, an anarchist, fires a shot at Clara Stuart, a famous stage and screen actress, but only wounds her. The star, through affectation and curiosity to know his motives, pleads in his favour at his trial, but he rebuffs her pity. After he has served 18 months in prison, they meet and fall in love.', 'Philippe Lutcher, an anarchist, fires a shot at Clara Stuart, a famous stage and screen actress, but only wounds her. The star, through affectation and curiosity to know his motives, pleads in his favour at his trial, but he rebuffs her pity. After he has served 18 months in prison, they meet and fall in love.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/u1xn0Obogkh0Qs5FdAbvthMy1hu.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:263768'),
